## Do While
A `do while` loop runs the code FIRST, then checks the condition. It always runs at least once.

```csharp
int i = 0;
do {
    Console.WriteLine(i);
    i++;
} while (i < 3);
// 0
// 1
// 2
```

Compare with `while`:
- `while` - checks THEN runs (might run 0 times)
- `do while` - runs THEN checks (always runs at least once)


